    "body": "## Summary\n- add a non-terminal `SUBMITTED` payout state for providers that accept a cash-out before terminal bank settlement is known\n- keep synchronous providers such as the explicit sandbox path compatible with direct `PROCESSING -> PAID`\n- add a provider-neutral, pessimistically locked settlement service keyed by the unique provider reference\n- deduplicate external settlement notifications by `(provider_code, provider_event_id)`\n- finalize `SUBMITTED -> PAID` without a second wallet debit\n- finalize `SUBMITTED -> FAILED` with the existing idempotent `PAYOUT_RESTORE` path\n- reject contradictory terminal provider events instead of rewriting financial history\n- add Flyway V45 with strict state/reference constraints and a private provider-event audit table\n- expose `SUBMITTED` clearly in worker/admin UI and extend payout smoke coverage/documentation\n\n## Financial invariants\n- wallet funds are debited exactly once at `PAYOUT_RESERVE`\n- provider acceptance creates no wallet transaction and never makes funds spendable again\n- a submitted payout is never automatically retried just because final bank settlement is slow\n- terminal `PAID` creates no second debit\n- terminal `FAILED` restores through the existing stable `payout:{id}:restore` operation key\n- replayed provider event IDs cannot mutate money twice\n- a matching later terminal event is audit-only; a contradictory terminal event is rejected\n\n## Security / privacy\n- this slice exposes no unauthenticated provider endpoint and stores no raw webhook body or Stripe secret\n- provider event persistence contains only bounded IDs, provider reference, coarse terminal outcome, normalized failure code and receive time\n- normal user payout DTO still does not expose provider references or internal failure metadata\n- admin actions remain available only for `REVIEW_REQUIRED`; `SUBMITTED` is display-only because manual retry could cause a duplicate payout\n\n## Stripe Connect boundary\nStripe distinguishes moving funds to a connected account from the connected account's bank payout, and bank payout completion is asynchronous. Therefore a future Stripe adapter must return `submitted(...)` when the operation is accepted and use signed `payout.paid` / `payout.failed` events or reconciliation to enter a terminal doFast state. This PR deliberately does **not** register live `stripe-connect` dispatch or add a public webhook endpoint yet.\n\n## Commits\n1. `payouts: model asynchronous provider settlement`\n2. `test: cover asynchronous payout settlement invariants`\n3. `payouts: expose asynchronous settlement state`\n\n## Required exact-head validation before merge\nHead: `6df3b1077cd8f550a8d5d2091b5cd952d54c88a1`\n\n- API/Maven verify\n- frontend production dependency audit + lint + build\n- containers/runtime smoke\n- Worker payout smoke with V45 and unchanged sandbox ledger lifecycle\n- web container health smoke when triggered\n\nDo not merge while any latest-head check is pending or failing. Any failure must be fixed on this same branch and the new head revalidated from scratch.",
